WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:05.449
Throughout its entire history,
mankind has witnessed many wars and border changes,

00:00:05.956 --> 00:00:09.014
the birth of empires and the rise of dictatorships.

00:00:09.691 --> 00:00:13.279
But a “genocide” has always been the most dreadful.

00:00:13.859 --> 00:00:16.314
It means the deliberate rejection of humanity,

00:00:16.952 --> 00:00:23.158
the purpose of destruction of people
for their beliefs, ethnicity, nationality, or race

00:00:23.795 --> 00:00:27.544
and, in fact, the annihilation of people for who they are.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.889
The Holodomor became one of the biggest crimes
against humanity in world history.

00:00:39.686 --> 00:00:47.122
As a result of Soviet policy in Ukraine in 1932–1933,
millions of people were killed.

00:00:48.078 --> 00:00:53.577
Ukrainians were starved to death
for their nationality, language, identity,

00:00:53.577 --> 00:00:57.469
and their denial to follow
that communist totalitarian machine

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:03.520
which forcibly led everyone to their fake
“bright future of communism” through blood and torture.

00:01:04.778 --> 00:01:11.578
On 30 December 1922, a new state was born
that united hundreds of nations and cultures

00:01:11.578 --> 00:01:19.156
by means of military interventions and revolution —
the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics (USSR).

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.816
Another name for this “union”
was “the prison of the nations”.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.090
Communism became a new policy,

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:33.011
the new ideology, religion, and culture
of this new state, its past and present.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:38.699
And in the meantime,
it became an excuse to kill millions of people.

00:01:39.528 --> 00:01:45.278
As a part of its economic policy,
the newly formed state set a course for collectivisation.

00:01:46.314 --> 00:01:51.621
Presented as creating “heaven on earth”,
in reality it turned into a forced organisation

00:01:51.621 --> 00:01:56.423
of private individual farmers
into collective farms owned by the state.

00:01:57.259 --> 00:02:03.256
In a utopian world, this was meant to become
a voluntary surrender of people’s own land and cattle;

00:02:03.993 --> 00:02:07.164
people were supposed to pass
all that property on to the state,

00:02:07.164 --> 00:02:13.865
to work collectively every day,
and then to distribute the produce among everyone who was working —

00:02:13.865 --> 00:02:15.939
according to the level of their contribution.

00:02:17.074 --> 00:02:20.672
The slogan was: “The one who does not work does not eat.”

00:02:21.589 --> 00:02:27.153
But the real motivation of the Soviet regime
was to rob and destroy Ukrainian villages.

00:02:28.706 --> 00:02:33.648
For farmers, their land and its cultivation
were the foundation of their well-being;

00:02:34.305 --> 00:02:36.480
their families’ prosperity depended on that.

00:02:37.572 --> 00:02:42.633
To surrender their land was to surrender the confidence
in their own future and their identity.

00:02:43.649 --> 00:02:48.370
This meant giving away everything they earned
through their hard work over several decades —

00:02:49.047 --> 00:02:53.770
giving it away to the state,
whose values and ideology were completely alien.

00:02:54.747 --> 00:03:01.858
And as a reward people would be allowed to exchange
their recorded “working days” for miserable food rations

00:03:01.858 --> 00:03:03.095
at the end of each year.

00:03:03.095 --> 00:03:08.328
Every ethnic group has its own specifics.

00:03:09.844 --> 00:03:11.077
Ukrainians  are proprietors.

00:03:13.013 --> 00:03:14.220
They are proprietors.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:20.844
You see, when we say...
when we use Stalin’s term “kurkul”(Ukr. for “kulak”)...

00:03:22.208 --> 00:03:28.804
If you look up the word “kurkul”
you’ll see that it means a “kite” (bird of prey).

00:03:30.418 --> 00:03:32.651
A bird that pounces on and swoops onto its prey.

00:03:33.135 --> 00:03:40.709
So they decided to use this metaphor of “kurkul”
as something predatory, sneaky;

00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:43.327
something that snatches and steals, and so on.

00:03:44.568 --> 00:03:47.160
But those whom they called “kurkuls”
were usual farm owners.

00:03:47.789 --> 00:03:51.937
Nearly 9 out of 10 Ukrainians lived in villages in those days.

00:03:51.937 --> 00:03:53.534
Most of them owned farms.

00:03:54.191 --> 00:04:00.399
They were not very enthusiastic about no longer
being independent farm owners but turning into “slaves”

00:04:00.399 --> 00:04:02.717
who would be working for food instead.

00:04:03.414 --> 00:04:11.234
So in the early 1930s there were over 4,000 protests
of Ukrainian farmers against such an initiative from the state.

00:04:11.971 --> 00:04:17.955
They refused to work for some abstract ideological constructs
while their children had nothing to eat.

00:04:18.832 --> 00:04:25.460
So their individualism and sense of national identity
became for the Soviet Union a stumbling block

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.460
at the gates to its collective heaven.

00:04:28.516 --> 00:04:34.585
That’s why by 1932 an unrealistic grain 
procurement plan
was set for Ukraine,

00:04:35.242 --> 00:04:38.967
imposing a quota of 356 million poods of grain.

00:04:39.525 --> 00:04:43.067
One pood is roughly 16.38 kg.

00:04:44.003 --> 00:04:47.617
This is an equivalent of about 5.8 million metric tonnes.

00:04:48.614 --> 00:04:51.829
So you can imagine how unrealistic such an amount was.

00:04:52.936 --> 00:05:00.293
To officially approve this plan,
Stalin’s closest associates — Kaganovich and Molotov — arrived in Kharkiv.

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:08.800
They were both clearly aware of Stalin’s intention
to destroy any existing opposition at all costs, especially in Ukraine.

00:05:09.116 --> 00:05:13.195
The Holodomor was civilizational annihilation of Ukrainians.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:18.673
The objectives of Adolf Hitler and Joseph Stalin were different.

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:26.205
Adolf Hitler’s objective — one of his major political goals —
was to fully destroy the Jewish people.

00:05:26.205 --> 00:05:29.294
Because this was a part of Nazism racial ideology.

00:05:30.548 --> 00:05:36.474
Joseph Stalin aimed to destroy
such a civilizational phenomenon as Ukrainians.

00:05:37.111 --> 00:05:45.000
To prevent the Ukrainian people from playing
their independent role in history

00:05:45.793 --> 00:05:48.253
and in civilisation ever again.

00:05:48.253 --> 00:05:53.375
That was because Russian chauvinists,
whom Stalin, despite being a Bolshevik, belonged to,

00:05:54.551 --> 00:06:01.660
were absolutely gutted with what was taking place
in Ukrainian land in 1917–1920.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:11.693
And even after that — when even under the Soviet occupation,
the party and economic elites continued conversations about independence.

00:06:11.693 --> 00:06:15.825
And at the same time,
the protests and resistance of the farmers continued.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:25.274
And it became clear to Stalin, who was a great expert in this,
if you destroy Ukrainian villages, physically wipe them out,

00:06:25.274 --> 00:06:32.054
you make it impossible for Ukrainian nation to develop.

00:06:32.054 --> 00:06:37.005
After the first waves of collectivisation,
farmers began to oppose it en masse —

00:06:37.901 --> 00:06:43.975
they were leaving collective farms (“kolhosps”),
taking back their inventory, cattle, and grain.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.508
On 7 August 1932 the resolution

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:52.723
“On Safekeeping the Property
of State Enterprises, Collective Farms

00:06:52.723 --> 00:06:57.684
and Cooperatives, and Strengthening Public
(Socialist) Property” was enacted.

00:06:59.013 --> 00:07:02.919
This document was better known 
as “the Law of Five Ears of Grain”.

00:07:03.943 --> 00:07:09.765
For the theft of any collective farm property,
the offenders could be executed by shooting;

00:07:10.442 --> 00:07:16.773
should they have any “extenuating circumstances”,
they could “get away” with imprisonment for at least 10 years.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:23.304
According to “the Law of Five Ears of Grain”,
people were not allowed to collect even crop residues.

00:07:24.339 --> 00:07:32.027
During that time special patrol brigades went from house to house
in a village to confiscate all grain people had.

00:07:33.421 --> 00:07:42.838
Molotov’s enthusiasm had no limits: by 18 November 1932
 he introduced blacklists, or so-called “black boards”.

00:07:43.714 --> 00:07:51.524
If a village entered such a list, it would become surrounded
by the army units, blocking entry into or exit from the village,

00:07:51.524 --> 00:07:59.076
taking away all essential goods from shops,
such as salt, matches, paraffin, and confiscating any food.

00:07:59.755 --> 00:08:05.215
In other words, it was a siege,
in which people would slowly starve to death.

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:12.050
The only territories where such a regime was introduced
were Ukraine and Kuban,

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:15.115
the territories mostly populated by Ukrainians.

00:08:16.131 --> 00:08:21.036
The Resolution of the Central Committee
of the All-Union Communist Party (Bolsheviks)

00:08:21.036 --> 00:08:27.027
and the Council of People’s Commissars of the USSR,
signed by Stalin and Molotov,

00:08:27.027 --> 00:08:34.530
isolated Ukrainians by preventing them from leaving
the Ukrainian SSR and Kuban to get any grain.

00:08:35.478 --> 00:08:43.474
During the spring and the early summer of 1933,
the highest rates of mortality were observed among the local population.

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:49.077
Nothing like this was done
to any other administrative region or Soviet Republic.

00:08:49.414 --> 00:08:58.880
In the sinister resolution,
which was signed by Stalin and Molotov on 14 December 1932,

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:09.440
titled “On Grain Procurement in Ukraine, North Caucasus and Western Region”,
which was the region of Smolensk those days...

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:14.581
It did not mention any reason
why the Smolensk region could not meet the procurement plan.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:21.127
Or what punishment the Smolensk region deserved
for not performing according to the plan.

00:09:21.127 --> 00:09:28.402
But the main reasons mentioned in that document
were the so-called “perpetrators” who allegedly infiltrated

00:09:28.402 --> 00:09:32.115
managerial positions at collective farms
and warehouses, and so on.

00:09:32.115 --> 00:09:35.528
Not only in Ukraine but also in Kuban.

00:09:36.305 --> 00:09:42.329
So the Smolensk region did not have
any penalties or punishment.

00:09:43.311 --> 00:09:49.379
But for the regions of Ukraine and the North Caucasus, 
which Kuban was, the document was very prescriptive.

00:09:50.477 --> 00:09:58.042
First it demanded to have public trials of a few secretaries

00:09:58.042 --> 00:10:01.556
and heads of the party local committee in Ukraine,
and sentence them to 5–10 years of imprisonment.

00:10:02.452 --> 00:10:06.313
And also, what’s important, to stop the Ukrainisation program.

00:10:06.313 --> 00:10:10.821
To cover the mass mortality,
Stalin deliberately manipulated the statistics.

00:10:11.737 --> 00:10:17.756
The world was presented with data
demonstrating high birth rates in the USSR in the early 1930s,

00:10:18.274 --> 00:10:24.640
whereas any facts about the catastrophic reduction
of the population in the Ukrainian SSR were concealed.

00:10:26.142 --> 00:10:29.232
Those who survived kept quiet for many decades.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.880
Otherwise they would risk their own safety
and the safety of their families and friends.

00:10:35.741 --> 00:10:41.049
The Soviet rule triumphed — 
the resistance of the population was broken down 

00:10:41.049 --> 00:10:44.145
by destroying anyone who had stood against.

00:10:45.123 --> 00:10:50.695
Any survivors were intimidated,
and they remembered well what could happen to those who opposed.

00:10:51.491 --> 00:10:56.874
They learned that no weapon was needed to kill —
the famine alone was enough.

00:10:57.673 --> 00:11:03.913
Many more years had passed before one of the biggest crimes 
against humanity became revealed to the world.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:10.954
By 2020 17 countries recognised 
the Holodomor as a form of genocide.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:15.819
Ukraine was among them, 
who had already done so in 2006.

00:11:16.755 --> 00:11:20.727
For Ukraine that meant deep rethinking of the country’s past,

00:11:20.727 --> 00:11:27.581
evaluation of the tragedy’s impact on the country’s present,
and definition of the course for future development.

00:11:28.518 --> 00:11:35.343
The Holodomor taught humanity the high price 
for silent inaction in the face of a global crime.

